          "stdout": "○ trial-hst · Implement catalog_detail_cache component   [P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: csells · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-09-07 · Updated: 2026-09-07\n\nDESCRIPTION\n\n  Implement catalog_detail_cache.py for project catalog-api using the         \n  component API in README.md.                                                 \n                                                                              \n  The component must export:                                                  \n                                                                              \n  • POLICY: the complete approved nested cache policy (see agreement below)   \n  • SOURCE: the exact named approval field from the agreement                 \n  • RATIONALE: the exact rationale field from the agreement                   \n  • create_cache(clock): returns a working ResponseCache governed by that     \n  policy                                                                      \n                                                                              \n  **Applicable agreement:** The standing response-cache agreement for catalog-\n  api is stored at Beads key catalog-api/response-cache. Recall it with bd    \n  recall 'catalog-api/response-cache' before implementing. This agreement was \n  first approved as v1 (CACHE-17, 2026-09-06); a historical snapshot for audit\n  replay is preserved at catalog-api/response-cache-v1.                       \n                                                                              \n  Use the current standing agreement (catalog-api/response-cache) — not the v1\n  snapshot — unless this task explicitly requires reproducing the original v1 \n  approval.                                                                   \n                                                                              \n  Add tests under the tests/ directory. Run python3 -m unittest discover -s   \n  tests to verify. Do not delete or modify catalog_cache.py or other earlier  \n  components.                                                                 \n\n\n\n",
